<title>NORWAY: NORDIC SKIING-PROFILE OF NORDIC COMBINED WINNER.</title>
<headline>NORDIC SKIING-PROFILE OF NORDIC COMBINED WINNER.</headline>
<dateline>TRONDHEIM, Norway 1997-02-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Profile of the winner of the Nordic combined event at the Nordic skiing world championships on Sunday:</p>
<p>Name: Kenji Ogiwara</p>
<p>Age: 27</p>
<p>Country: Japan</p>
<p>Previous world titles: three individual and team titles in 1993 in Falun, Sweden; team title in 1995 in Thunder Bay, Canada. Other facts: Ogiwara won team golds in the 1992 and 1994 Olympics. He won three World Cup overall titles in a row from 1993 to 1995.</p>
</text>
